So for capacity, just a simple compact disk

00:00:59.240 --> 00:01:02.920
can handle one hour of music,

00:01:02.920 --> 00:01:07.920
and that is equivalent of 6 billion binary digits,

00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:12.520
which is an amazing amount of data, if you think of it.

00:01:12.520 --> 00:01:25.400
Another important thing is both digital designs are very immune to noise, both for their sending

00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:35.880
and receiving, but also for storing and retrieving the data. If you think about movies, at the

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:43.640
beginning of movie making business most movies were made just I mean all the

00:01:43.640 --> 00:01:49.720
movies were made analog so what happened with those tapes because of wear and

00:01:49.720 --> 00:01:56.040
tear and just because of simple aging there was damage of information on the

00:01:56.040 --> 00:02:02.280
tape which we call in you know engineering systems we call that noise so

00:02:02.280 --> 00:02:08.680
those movies did not look very well if they played from the same tape several

00:02:08.680 --> 00:02:18.280
hundreds or thousands of times. However, for digital movies and most analog movies

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:24.600
have been digitalized at the end for storing and safekeeping, if we even have

00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:29.400
the noise we can make a technology such that if we have a noise and noise is

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:38.520
between certain level, we can retrieve the information perfectly. Similar is applied

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:47.520
to transmission. While you are transmitting your data, the data on the reception can have

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:54.400
certain amount of degradation due to noise. So, we are transmitting a sequence of zeros

00:02:54.400 --> 00:03:00.640
and ones, and some of these zeros and ones can be corrupted and change their values,

00:03:00.640 --> 00:03:05.360
so basically flip from zero to one and one to zero.

00:03:05.360 --> 00:03:12.300
We have mechanisms in digital systems that we can reconstruct the original information

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:17.000
even when there is some amount of noise, and these are called error correction and

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:20.000
error detection mechanisms.

