00:05:49.610 --> 00:05:52.450
So what are the digital circuits?

00:05:52.450 --> 00:05:54.930
The digital circuit is going to be a circuit

00:05:54.930 --> 00:05:56.970
to use binary digits.

00:05:56.970 --> 00:06:01.650
And binary digits, they're called binary

00:06:01.650 --> 00:06:04.870
because they have up to two states that they can assume.

00:06:06.350 --> 00:06:11.350
So the digital circuits are usually made out of logic gate.

00:06:12.210 --> 00:06:15.610
And usually those circuits are very complex

00:06:15.610 --> 00:06:19.190
and they are made out of large number of this logic gate.

00:06:19.190 --> 00:06:21.910
And the logic gate are the ones that are operating

00:06:21.910 --> 00:06:24.390
along those binary variables.

00:06:24.390 --> 00:06:26.790
These are the variables, binary digits

00:06:26.790 --> 00:06:29.510
or binary variables that have two states.

00:06:31.790 --> 00:06:35.510
However, the binary, the logic gate

00:06:35.510 --> 00:06:40.510
is small and simple electronic representation of a function.

00:06:44.590 --> 00:06:46.870
Usually people call it Boolean logic functions

00:06:46.870 --> 00:06:48.830
or logic function.

00:06:48.830 --> 00:06:53.110
And we will learn those functions and how to deal with that.

00:06:53.110 --> 00:06:55.230
So that's going to be theoretical framework

00:06:55.230 --> 00:06:58.110
for lots of our work in this course.

00:06:58.110 --> 00:07:01.390
This is going to be Boolean or logic algebra

00:07:01.390 --> 00:07:02.590
that it will deal with.

00:07:03.910 --> 00:07:06.270
So let's go back to the gates.

00:07:06.270 --> 00:07:08.430
They implement those logic functions.

00:07:08.430 --> 00:07:11.210
And those logic functions can be something called

00:07:11.210 --> 00:07:12.630
and or and not.

00:07:12.630 --> 00:07:15.230
And we'll see that in the first couple of weeks

00:07:15.230 --> 00:07:17.310
in our class.

00:07:17.310 --> 00:07:21.190
but they are usually implemented to use the smallest,

00:07:21.190 --> 00:07:23.710
the fewest number of transistors

00:07:23.710 --> 00:07:28.710
because we want them to have smaller size,

00:07:29.070 --> 00:07:30.910
power and cost,

00:07:30.910 --> 00:07:35.430
and yet to keep or increase their reliability.

00:07:35.430 --> 00:07:42.220
What that means is that each gate

00:07:45.300 --> 00:07:49.180
consists of a few transistors,

00:07:49.180 --> 00:07:51.220
So they are implementing just kind of,

00:07:51.220 --> 00:07:53.180
let's call it basic functions.

00:07:54.500 --> 00:07:59.500
Now, in general, when we look at logic design,

00:07:59.500 --> 00:08:02.340
we have something that is called feature size.

00:08:02.340 --> 00:08:05.340
Feature size or technology node,

00:08:05.340 --> 00:08:08.860
as you are going to see somewhere in the literature,

00:08:08.860 --> 00:08:13.580
that means that tells us how 10 is the tennis line

00:08:13.580 --> 00:08:15.520
that makes the transistor.

00:08:15.520 --> 00:08:29.520
So each transistor is part of a gate and several transistors are implementing those gates and we're going to use gates as basic blocks to build other stuff.

00:08:29.520 --> 00:08:40.520
Now more slow, and maybe some of you are familiar with them, that it says that chips double their density in every 18 months.

00:08:40.520 --> 00:08:41.520
What does that mean?

00:08:41.520 --> 00:08:48.760
the same area of a chip is going to have two times more transistors every 18

00:08:48.760 --> 00:08:56.720
months and that is because there is a new finer technology or technology

00:08:56.720 --> 00:09:03.440
node with smaller feature size and basically there is ability to pack more

00:09:03.440 --> 00:09:16.220
and more transistors on the same chip. Because we can reduce the total size of each transistor

00:09:16.220 --> 00:09:24.800
and each gate, in general, devices that have digital circuits become smaller, but also

00:09:24.800 --> 00:09:31.120
they become faster and cheaper to design. Nowadays, there are hundreds of millions,

00:09:31.120 --> 00:09:39.160
And actually, nowadays, I saw the last generation of 14 generation of Intel processors, and

00:09:39.160 --> 00:09:44.040
they had up to a few billions of gates, which is an enormous amount.

